From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:25:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] busybox: printf: no arithmetic on a null pointer

printf's print_direc() subtracts one from the place of the conversion's
'*', which strchr() gives as NULL when there is none: undefined
behaviour, which traps in every printf without a '*' when the build
sanitizes with -fsanitize-trap. The init scripts use printf, so a
UBSan build's boot traps hundreds of times.

Add a patch to busybox that compares only when there is a '*'. It is
meant for busybox upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/utils/busybox/Makefile                |  2 +-
 ...-do-not-subtract-from-a-null-pointer.patch | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/utils/busybox/patches/800-printf-do-not-subtract-from-a-null-pointer.patch

diff --git a/package/utils/busybox/Makefile b/package/utils/busybox/Makefile
index a950cff..bb00d33 100644
--- a/package/utils/busybox/Makefile
+++ b/package/utils/busybox/Makefile
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=busybox
 PKG_VERSION:=1.38.0
-PKG_RELEASE:=3
+PKG_RELEASE:=4
 PKG_FLAGS:=essential
 
 PKG_SOURCE:=$(PKG_NAME)-$(PKG_VERSION).tar.bz2
diff --git a/package/utils/busybox/patches/800-printf-do-not-subtract-from-a-null-pointer.patch b/package/utils/busybox/patches/800-printf-do-not-subtract-from-a-null-pointer.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aa719df
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/utils/busybox/patches/800-printf-do-not-subtract-from-a-null-pointer.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] printf: do not subtract from a null pointer
+
+print_direc() tells a '*' for the width from the one of ".*" by comparing
+the place of the first '*' less one with that of ".*". In a conversion
+without a '*', strchr() returns NULL, and the comparison subtracts one
+from a null pointer, which is undefined behaviour. Built with
+-fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined, every printf whose
+format has no '*' traps.
+
+Compare only when the conversion has a '*'.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/coreutils/printf.c
++++ b/coreutils/printf.c
+@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@
+ 
+ 	have_prec = strstr(format, ".*");
+ 	have_width = strchr(format, '*');
+-	if (have_width - 1 == have_prec)
++	if (have_width && have_width - 1 == have_prec)
+ 		have_width = NULL;
+ 
+ 	/* multiconvert sets errno = 0, but %s needs it cleared */
